# .cto/devteam-model — the model ORCHESTRATED windows run on.
#
# Copy to `.cto/devteam-model` to change it. With no file, the built-in default
# `opus` applies, which is what you want if the answer is "the account default".
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Claude Code's /model picker changes the window you type it
# in AND saves the choice as the machine-global default for every session started
# afterwards. A launcher that passes no model inherits that — which is how a Fable
# pick in a CTO window ended up running three dev tabs on 2026-09-02 (see
# docs/memos/2026-09-03-rca-handoff-model-inheritance.md). `claude --model X` is
# scoped to the session it launches and writes nothing back, so pinning here means
# the CEO can pick freely in the CTO window without it reaching the fleet.
#
# Consumed by scripts/cto/resolve-devteam-model.sh, which /handoff,
# /resume-dev-team and qa-drive-claude.sh all resolve through.
# Precedence: DEVTEAM_MODEL env var > this file > built-in `opus`.

# ── the fleet default: first bare line wins ──────────────────────────────────
# Prefer an ALIAS — it tracks the latest model of that family. A pinned full name
# silently ages into a retired one.
opus

# Use a full name only for a variant an alias does not select — e.g. the 1M-context
# build, which is worth it for long sprints but must be revisited each model release:
#   claude-opus-5[1m]

# ── optional per-repo overrides, one per line ────────────────────────────────
#   acme-tuner=fable
#   acme-demo-app=sonnet

# ── opt out entirely (NOT recommended) ───────────────────────────────────────
# `inherit` passes no --model flag and restores the pre-2026-09-03 behaviour:
# every tab takes whatever /model last saved, in any window, silently.
#   inherit
